WEBVTT

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
The Human World Annihilated!

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.550
Yggdrasil's Decision

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.770
The Human World Annihilated!

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.550
Yggdrasil's Decision!

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:17.550
Activating the true power of the Burst Mode, Masaru and ShineGreymon defeated Belphemon.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:25.810
However, using the last of his strength, Kurata detonated a space-time oscillation bomb,

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:31.370
demolishing the dimensional barrier that separated Earth from the Digital World.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.380
This is...

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.550
The dimensional barrier...

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:14.900
It's destroyed...

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.410
Damn it!

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:19.620
That Kurata made a nuisance of himself to the very end.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.670
This is the worst thing that's ever happened in history.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.840
The Digital World is falling on us...

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.390
Damn it!

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:32.750
It's not possible for two worlds to exist in one dimension.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.010
If this keeps up, both our world and the Digital World...

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.470
will be obliterated.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.020
Obliterated?!

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.040
Yggdrasil.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.390
Yggdrasil!

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.540
Craniummon...

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.050
has arrived at your command.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:10.430
Craniummon

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:10.430
Ultimate Level

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:05.870
Craniummon.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.440
An Ultimate Level Digimon.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.430
He's one of the Royal Knights who protect the Digital World.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.090
I've been waiting for you.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.780
Grant me the honor of your words.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:32.700
Both the Digital World and human world are now entering a disastrous state of affairs.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.210
It is inevitable that the existence of the two worlds will destroy each other

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.240
and that both parties will be annihilated.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.060
Is there no way we can avoid the collision?

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.300
There is... one way.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:48.600
What may that be?

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.410
We can remove the human world first.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.060
Then the collision itself will never happen.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.520
What?

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:02.530
If there is a way for one of us to survive, then it is illogical for both to perish.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.990
Then what shall be done about the humans?

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.950
They will also be eliminated.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:16.570
The humans have continued to make mistakes without even reflecting on the error of their ways.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.710
Are you saying... that they deserve to be killed?

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:22.560
Their existence does no good and only causes plenty of harm.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:28.240
The billions of lives that make up the human species will be annihilated.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.680
Are you certain about your decision?

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:31.640
Then...

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.680
You shall see for youself

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:38.070
whether there is any worth for these human beings to survive!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.860
Everything began when the humans perceived the existence of the Digital World.

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:49.910
A world which they were never originally meant to interact with.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:55.100
But the humans' intellectual curiosity would not leave things be.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.580
They forcibly tried to link the two worlds together.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.620
By doing so, their inquisitive spirits invited disaster.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.330
Ikuto!

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:15.810
Watch out!

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:17.690
Ikuto!

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:20.100
Ikuto!!

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.240
After many attempts, the humans finally entered the Digital World.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.930
Then they began to eliminate Digimon without justification.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.280
S-Stay away from me!

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.410
Stay away!

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.110
Don't shoot, Kurata!

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:37.870
Throw your gun down!

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:43.970
In addition,

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:51.680
they destroyed the equilibrium between the human world and the Digital World by placing greater significance on their own lives.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:53.830
Now that it's come to this...

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.460
That's...

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:58.850
The space-time oscillation bomb.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:04.440
We can use this to force the Digital Gate to open!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.240
This is the only choice we have if we want to survive!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.650
The humans are indeed selfish beings.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:21.890
However...

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:24.090
Is it necessary to go so far as to exterminate them?

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.760
Then remember the worst day our world has experienced.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.230
It's showtime!

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:05.370
Yukidarumon!

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:08.160
Yukidarumon!

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:10.620
Ikuto, don't come here!

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:11.530
Run!

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.790
Yukidarumon!!!

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:25.950
Even so, I continued to watch over the humans.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:31.360
I wanted to be certain whether or not these human beings truly were a baneful existence.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:43.990
Holy crap!

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.930
What the hell are you doing? Move!

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.590
Please keep calm and take refuge!

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:51.590
Hurry!

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:05.340
Damn it!

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.580
There's no end to this!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:12.930
Mayday! Mayday!

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.700
This is MCC 17012.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:16.880
We're going down!

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:17.910
I repeat, we're going down!

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:19.660
Damn it...

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:20.730
Captain!

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:37.510
Isn't there a way we can prevent the collision?

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:38.680
No!

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:43.340
The boundary that separates space-time is collapsing at an alarming rate!

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:44.700
It's impossible to stop it!

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:47.520
Then wouldn't it be safer on the opposite side of Earth?

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:50.820
Thinking in three dimensions like that is meaningless!

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:53.870
This thing is rushing towards Earth itself!

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.870
It's a disaster that's reached a super-dimensional scale!

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:02.320
The dimensional wall grew even more unstable,

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:05.800
and Digimon started falling one after the other into the human world.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:18.340
That is because the humans continuously experimented on the Digital Gate for no good reason.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:26.010
The Digimon, confused under the influence of human desires, went berserk against their own will.

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:27.220
However,

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:30.260
there are Digimon who have sided with the humans.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.770
Do you mean DATS?

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:32.980
Yes.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:35.070
Of course,

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:41.460
their efforts to prevent unnecessary fighting between the humans and Digimon are worthy of evaluation.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:48.470
After all, they did turn the Digimon back into Digieggs and sent them back to their proper place.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:56.450
However, that is overshadowed by the act of humans modifying Digimon to be used as weapons,

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:59.510
and proceeding to slaughter other Digimon one after the other.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:02.470
That is indeed inexcusable.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.070
I told you to get lost!

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:29.530
By now, you should know who you are really supposed to hate.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:30.930
Mercurimon!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.450
Ikuto...

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:34.590
Live...

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:38.090
as a human with a Digimon's heart.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:09.370
Mercurimon!

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:11.890
Why did you help us?!

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:17.780
I wanted to try believing once more...

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:21.940
in what your father, Daimon Suguru, said...

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:26.400
That a time will come when humans and Digimon can live together in harmony.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.610
Harmony between humans and Digimon?

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.960
That day will never come!

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:46.540
I-Ikuto...!

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:48.230
Be strong...!

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.230
MERCURIMON!

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.830
That's not all.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:06.220
They even found legitimacy in using repulsive and evil means, such as fusing humans and Digimon together, to gain power.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.140
Hyper Bio Evolution!

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.440
BioThunderbirmon!

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.820
BioCoatlmon!

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.360
BioStegomon!

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:29.030
What's more, they attacked the Holy Capital to collect the Digimon's life energy.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:32.200
Drop the Gizmon Javelin.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:13.330
And finally...

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:20.540
They revived Belphemon, who long ago had almost brought the Digital World to ruin.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:27.540
Yes!

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:33.720
I will become the king who will rule over both this world and the Digital World!

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:48.530
I'll just have to turn into Belphemon's heart myself!

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:04.090
What's that?

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:26.720
In the end, they have trapped both their own world and the Digital World on the path leading to their self-destruction.

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:38.110
Why do you, as father and son, continue to stand before me?!

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:39.730
If only you two weren't around...!

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:42.000
If only you two weren't around...!

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:47.340
I would have easily been able to rise to the top of the world!!!

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:52.040
D-D-DAIMON!!!

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:06.800
Charge!

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:11.510
Digisoul Burst!

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:15.910
ShineGreymon!

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:17.430
Burst Mode!

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:27.290
DAIMON!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:45.170
I won't allow this!

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:02.870
Stay away from me!

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:06.540
Stay away!

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:09.450
This will finish you, Kurata!

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.630
KURATA!

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:37.100
My dreams...

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:39.450
They're not finished...

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.200
My ambitions...

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.790
They're not over yet!

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.450
Wh-What is this?

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:52.700
This is...

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:53.420
It can't be!

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:55.130
No...

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:56.090
Impossible!

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.590
Why is this happening?!

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:00.050
Ravemon!

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:00.880
Okay!

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:03.980
H-H-Help me!

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:05.940
I'm... still...!

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.750
Still...!

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:14.610
Just as I thought, the humans do not deserve to live.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.900
If that is your will, Yggdrasil,

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:20.320
the Royal Knights shall obey.

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:23.160
I'm counting on you.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:36.460
Damn it...

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.880
Are you really sure we can't do anything?

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:44.640
Masaru!

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:46.520
Over there!

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:51.480
That's...!

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:07.580
NOTE: The characters on BanchouLeomon's jacket say "Throughout Heaven and Earth," referring to the Buddha quote he said in his first appearance.

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:24.390
That's...

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:29.310
BanchouLeomon!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.770
He's slowing down the Digital World with his Digisoul!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.110
Is that even possible?

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:38.890
I've unleashed all of my Digisoul!

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:43.570
In moments, I will become the stone foundation that will support the Digital World!

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:45.160
What?

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:46.660
Masaru!

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.120
Go to Yggdrasil!

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.120
Before my life runs out!

00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:53.300
Yggdrasil?

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:56.590
You mean that God of the Digital World who my dad went to find?

00:18:56.950 --> 00:19:01.450
From this point on, you will face even greater calamities!

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:05.530
In order to resolve them, you must meet Yggdrasil!

00:19:05.530 --> 00:19:10.100
Since you are Suguru's son, you should be able to do it!

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.150
Masaru!

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:21.140
I'm leaving it in your hands!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.120
It stopped...

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:48.650
Aniki!

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:16.670
BANCHOULEOMON!

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:39.480
Let's go, ShineGreymon.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:40.900
To the Digital World.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:42.060
Yeah.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:44.210
Wait a second!

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:45.610
How are you going to get there?

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:48.290
It's right there in front of us.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:50.790
We can just fly straight towards it.

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:52.300
It's too dangerous!

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.890
The dimensional barrier has crumbled!

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:57.500
We don't know what condition the skies are in right now!

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:03.830
BanchouLeomon is risking his life to support the Digital World!

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:07.470
We've got to show the same amount of guts that he's shown!

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.540
Let's go, Masaru!

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:14.770
To the Digital World!

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:17.060
Let's go, Master.

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:19.770
I'm more than ready for a little danger.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:22.780
All right.

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:26.240
It may be better than waiting here for our deaths.

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:29.210
Then it's decided.

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:31.400
Let's go!

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:32.330
Yeah!

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:32.330
Yeah!

